"Long summer is placed at the seam between summer and autumn, roughly the humid, heavy transition period after summer's peak heat but before autumn's dry, crisp air sets in — a stretch of weather that, fittingly, is often described using the same damp-heat pattern covered in an earlier unit. This isn't a coincidence: earth's association with transformation and dampness, tied to the spleen's role in processing food and fluids, matches this specific stretch of the calendar better than it would match any of the other four seasons.": "e6f108550ac7",
"Long summer's placement — squeezed between two other seasons rather than granted an equal one-fifth share of the year — mirrors earth's own position in the five-element cycle: not one of four elements pointing outward in four directions, but a stabilizing presence at the center and in between. The calendar, in this small detail, is built to match the theory exactly, rather than the theory being stretched afterward to fit a calendar that was never designed with five parts in mind.": "c6a02710b663",
